# Keeps secrets and local state out of the Docker build context.
#
# The Dockerfiles in infrastructure/docker/ run `COPY . .` from the repository
# root. Without this file the root `.env` (database passwords, JWT secrets,
# provider keys) would be sent to the builder and baked into a build layer.
# Production configuration is supplied as environment variables at run time.

# Secrets and local configuration
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Version control and editor state
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
.claude

# Dependencies and build output (rebuilt inside the image)
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.pnpm-store

# Local data
**/uploads
*.log
